      <activity id="5fe1f1d6-4952-5ecb-843f-59b6f96ecfdb" activityNameId="06fd43de-c883-51fe-9b15-0ec90ac8a26a" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Heat, residential, by conversion of hydrogen using fuel cell, PEM, allocated by exergy, distributed by pipe [ebc70bf5b7]</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Heat, residential, by conversion of hydrogen using fuel cell, PEM, allocated by exergy, distributed by pipeline, produced by Auto-thermal reforming using natural gas from Switzerland
This dataset represents the supply of 1 megajoule of heat in a residence, by hydrogen conversion in a fuel cell, PEM. The hydrogen is produced by  Auto-thermal reforming, with natural gas from Switzerland as feedstock. Heat conversion efficiency [% LHV input]: 50%. LHV [MJ/kg]: 120. Market price [Euro/MJ]: 0.03. Synthesis efficiency [% LHV input]: 0%. Total cap. Input-related [kW]: 2.74. CO2 biogenic share [%]: 0%. Power [kW]: 1.6. Lifetime [years]: 4.88. Annual operation [hours]: 4100. Allocation factor: 0.12. On-site storage loss [%]: 0. Use loss [%]: 0.56. For more information, refer to: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023. Source: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023.

 UUID: 2f1f5262-2098-3d2e-8789-a71dac9e36ff
Location: 
